# Database & security

## Schema standards

- UUID primary keys on all tables.
- Foreign keys for every relationship; indexes on FKs and common filters.
- Unique constraints where business identity requires them.
- `created_at` / `updated_at` with triggers to maintain them.
- Same-gym invariants via composite FKs or triggers (related rows must share `gym_id`).
- Amounts are integer paise (`bigint`) and must be `>= 0`.
- Payments are append-only; corrections are reversal rows, never updates/deletes of payment amounts.

## RLS & provisioning

- RLS enabled on every table; policies go through a security-definer role helper (never trust client `gym_id`).
- No client inserts into `gyms` or `user_gym_roles`.
- Provisioning only via a service-role-only function (e.g. `provision_gym`).
- Never disable RLS. No service-role key in the app.

## Tests

- pgTAP cross-tenant tests covering read, insert, update, and delete isolation between gyms.
